WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:09.465
The Sponsorship Scandal: one hundred million dollars in fraudulent contracts funneled to Liberal-friendly advertising agencies between 1996 and 2004.

00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:16.022
The Gomery Commission Phase 2 Report, released February 2006, found explicit criminal conspiracy.

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:19.727
Jean Brault: convicted and sentenced to thirty months.

00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:23.977
Charles Guité: convicted and sentenced to forty-two months in prison.

00:00:23.977 --> 00:00:32.249
SNC-Lavalin: the Prime Minister's Office applied eleven documented instances of inappropriate pressure on Attorney General Jody Wilson-Raybould.

00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:36.624
Katie Telford, Gerald Butts, and Michael Wernick orchestrated the campaign.

00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:44.693
The Aga Khan vacation in December 2016 breached sections 11, 12, and 21 of the Conflict of Interest Act.

00:00:44.693 --> 00:00:46.409
These are not allegations.

00:00:46.409 --> 00:00:48.252
These are findings of fact.

00:00:48.252 --> 00:00:52.943
The WE Charity scandal: a nine hundred and twelve million dollar sole-source contract.

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:59.022
The Trudeau family received over three hundred and twelve thousand dollars in speaking fees from the same organization.

00:00:59.022 --> 00:01:06.806
RCMP Commissioner Lucki promised the Minister's office and the PMO firearms information to support Bill C-21 in May 2020.

00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:12.727
Every scandal follows the same architecture — public money, private benefit, institutional cover.
